From a372ea507671d8898724a55a1648eb8a9e51b863 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:48:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] Sum the accumulated fields over 3h/6h steps;
 precipitation factors by hemisphere

At 3h or 6h time steps the accumulated surface fields (tp, ssrd, strd...)
were the ERA5 hour ending at each stamp: precipitation was that hour times
the step and radiation the mean of the last hour. fetch_era5_to_zarr now
fetches them hourly (CDS: all hours, plus the last hours of the previous
day in a small second request; GDEX: the hours of the windows) and the
store holds their sums over the step ending at the stamp (store attribute
accumulation_hours, part of the request). The downscaler reads that
attribute (1 h by default), sums an hourly store downscaled at 3h or 6h,
warns for a store sampling the hours, and the accumulation window of the
solar geometry follows. Split downloads are merged with an outer join.

The monthly precipitation coefficients of MicroMet, derived in the
Northern Hemisphere, are shifted by six months for points south of the
equator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012FMkEYDUJxvxmd3SbUsJfP
